WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:06.190
Drawn by a landscape as white as snow,

00:00.850 --> 00:06.190
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:06.240 --> 00:12.740
I'm headed toward an unseen world.

00:06.240 --> 00:12.740
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:18.460 --> 00:21.680
I've been traveling while lost

00:18.460 --> 00:21.680
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:21.710 --> 00:24.470
Under this gray sky.

00:21.710 --> 00:24.460
Nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:24.500 --> 00:30.560
Every day with new maps, stained with my many dreams.

00:24.500 --> 00:30.560
Higawari no chizu ikutsumo no yume ga nijindeita

00:30.560 --> 00:32.950
I wonder if someday,

00:30.560 --> 00:32.950
Itsuka wa sa

00:32.970 --> 00:36.990
Even with these tiny steps of mine,

00:32.970 --> 00:36.990
Chippoke na boku no kono hohaba demo

00:37.010 --> 00:43.070
I'll be able to travel beyond those clouds.

00:37.010 --> 00:43.070
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:43.070 --> 00:44.700
I put on a bold front.

00:43.070 --> 00:44.700
Tsuyogatte

00:44.700 --> 00:46.250
End up hurting myself.

00:44.700 --> 00:46.250
Kizutsuita

00:46.280 --> 00:49.330
I feel empty inside.

00:46.280 --> 00:49.330
Kokoro sukashita youni

00:49.330 --> 00:50.870
It's started to rain,

00:49.330 --> 00:50.870
Furidashita

00:50.870 --> 00:53.040
And the raindrops

00:50.870 --> 00:53.040
Amatsubu tachi ga

00:53.040 --> 00:56.260
Began to repeat their scattered reflections.

00:53.040 --> 00:56.260
Ranhansha kurikaesu

00:56.280 --> 00:59.130
These straight rays of light

00:56.280 --> 00:59.130
Massugu na hikari ga

00:59.130 --> 01:01.850
Start to cross one another.

00:59.130 --> 01:01.850
Kousa shite

01:01.880 --> 01:05.430
And without telling anyone where they're headed,

01:01.880 --> 01:05.430
Yakusaki mo tsugenumama

01:05.430 --> 01:06.720
Across the endless distances,

01:05.430 --> 01:06.720
Doko made mo

01:06.720 --> 01:08.310
They pass through all matter.

01:06.720 --> 01:08.310
Tsukinukeru

01:08.330 --> 01:14.140
I burn these faint afterimages onto my eyes.

01:08.330 --> 01:14.140
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakitsukete

01:14.140 --> 01:16.060
Under this sky,

01:14.140 --> 01:16.060
Kono sora no shita

01:16.060 --> 01:19.890
Wherever I am,

01:16.060 --> 01:19.890
Donna toko ni itemo

01:20.310 --> 01:22.190
I should be able to reach

01:20.310 --> 01:22.190
Todoku hazu nanda

01:22.190 --> 01:27.000
The unseen world.

01:22.190 --> 01:27.000
Mada minu sekai e

01:35.650 --> 01:37.360
That was so exhausting!

01:37.650 --> 01:39.950
They were watching us the whole time, too.

01:39.950 --> 01:42.240
Mr. Fu and Ran Fan, right?

01:42.240 --> 01:43.160
Hey!

01:43.700 --> 01:44.870
Where's the young master!?

01:49.330 --> 01:50.330
I don't see him...

01:50.500 --> 01:52.840
Could he have gone missing again?

01:54.800 --> 01:57.840
Seriously... The instant I take my eyes off him...

01:59.260 --> 02:00.680
Young master!

02:00.680 --> 02:02.850
Where have you gone?!

02:04.140 --> 02:05.850
I hope he hasn't collapsed somewhere like last time...

02:05.850 --> 02:08.390
Good riddance.

02:08.390 --> 02:09.180
Let's go.

02:10.190 --> 02:11.400
Okay...

02:14.060 --> 02:17.480
Young master! Where are you?!

02:26.830 --> 02:29.540
There's something... odd about this country.

02:29.980 --> 02:32.980
Footsteps of a 
Comrade-in-Arms

02:29.980 --> 02:32.980
Footsteps of a 
Comrade-in-Arms

02:44.090 --> 02:46.010
It's me. I came to visit.

02:48.140 --> 02:49.310
Good work.

02:50.270 --> 02:51.520
From the Colonel.

02:54.690 --> 02:56.520
Yo, it's the cigarette kid!

02:56.730 --> 02:59.150
How are you doing? Were you even able to beat him once?

02:59.150 --> 03:00.440
Not a chance.

03:00.440 --> 03:02.780
This game is pretty boring, too.

03:03.030 --> 03:06.450
Hey, I can go cut people up if it's just at night, right?

03:06.450 --> 03:07.870
Of course not!

03:07.870 --> 03:12.000
Then, could you at least... bring that Hawkeye lady?

03:12.000 --> 03:14.580
Yeah, I'll mention it to her.

03:15.330 --> 03:19.670
How much longer do I have to watch over this guy?

03:20.130 --> 03:21.170
What did the Colonel say?

03:22.670 --> 03:26.010
"Sorry for putting you in charge of such a dangerous task."

03:26.510 --> 03:28.560
"Don't worry about military duty, though."

03:28.560 --> 03:30.770
"I've marked you down as absent due to illness."

03:31.560 --> 03:38.230
"However, you're as good as dead if a civilian
or someone from the military besides us finds you."

03:38.230 --> 03:39.270
...is what he said.

03:41.320 --> 03:44.110
Any good news?

03:44.570 --> 03:45.280
Yup.

03:45.280 --> 03:46.700
Huh? What is it?

03:47.320 --> 03:49.660
I got a girlfriend!

03:49.870 --> 03:53.750
She really helped me out when I was struggling with the transfer and all.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.080
She's such a babe, too!

03:56.080 --> 03:59.170
Hey, do you think I'd enjoy cutting her up?

03:59.880 --> 04:02.260
Just go home already...

04:02.260 --> 04:03.050
Oh my.

04:03.050 --> 04:04.510
What's wrong with him?

04:04.510 --> 04:06.470
Hey, are you all right?

04:04.510 --> 04:05.720
Is he okay?

04:06.640 --> 04:08.600
F-Food...

04:08.600 --> 04:10.760
He's completely out of it.

04:11.390 --> 04:12.640
Where's he from?

04:13.390 --> 04:15.520
What? You came from Xing?

04:16.230 --> 04:18.020
That's so far...

04:18.360 --> 04:20.400
By the way, where's your certificate of entry?

04:23.990 --> 04:25.490
Make way! Make way!

04:25.490 --> 04:27.530
Illegal entrant coming through!

04:27.990 --> 04:30.780
Young master! Where are you?!

04:31.080 --> 04:34.290
He's passed out somewhere... I just know he has!

04:35.040 --> 04:39.000
Well, let's go say hi to the military first.

04:39.000 --> 04:40.040
Let's.

04:40.590 --> 04:44.590
Then... I think I'll go visit Mr. Hughes' place first.

04:45.220 --> 04:48.090
I can't wait to see Miss Gracia and Elicia, either.

04:48.090 --> 04:49.470
Okay.

04:49.470 --> 04:51.390
We'll head over there afterwards.

04:51.390 --> 04:52.850
Well, see you then.

04:57.020 --> 05:02.230
I wonder if Lt. Colonel Hughes uncovered
more information about the stone for us since then.

05:03.320 --> 05:06.110
Well, the Führer President warned him to stay out of it, too.

05:07.070 --> 05:10.280
Let's give him the information we obtained, first.

05:11.620 --> 05:12.780
Homunculus...

05:13.040 --> 05:13.910
Yeah.

05:14.700 --> 05:18.000
The Lt. Colonel should be at the military chambers...

05:19.580 --> 05:20.540
Over there!

05:38.850 --> 05:39.730
Sheska?

05:40.350 --> 05:40.980
Sheska!

05:41.860 --> 05:42.770
Yes?

05:42.770 --> 05:45.110
You have the key to that room, right?

05:45.280 --> 05:46.780
Yes, I do.

05:46.990 --> 05:49.320
Oh... Room 3, you mean?

05:49.320 --> 05:51.700
I've kind of made a mess in there...

05:52.030 --> 05:55.200
Don't worry about it. I just need to grab some documents.

05:55.200 --> 05:57.040
I'm telling you, it's not all right.

05:57.040 --> 05:59.210
I'll clean it up right away, so please give me a moment!

06:01.080 --> 06:05.050
Okay. I'll come get it later, so please finish by then.

06:05.050 --> 06:05.960
Y-Yes, ma'am!

06:20.730 --> 06:23.060
Umm... Colonel?

06:23.690 --> 06:24.900
Colonel Mustang.

06:29.610 --> 06:33.120
How many minutes was I asleep?

06:33.120 --> 06:34.660
I'd say about ten.

06:39.120 --> 06:40.790
I don't have much time before the army council.

06:41.710 --> 06:47.920
Excuse my unsolicited advice, but perhaps
you should rest instead of straining yourself?

06:47.920 --> 06:49.880
Yeah, I'll come again.

06:53.760 --> 06:55.470
Was that Colonel Mustang?

06:57.430 --> 07:00.480
G-Good morning, Captain Focker!

07:00.480 --> 07:02.350
Morning, Sheska.

07:02.980 --> 07:05.690
But why was the Colonel here?

07:05.690 --> 07:08.110
W-Well... you see...

07:08.110 --> 07:09.690
The door to the archives is open, too.

07:09.690 --> 07:12.110
I'm sorry! The truth is, well...

07:13.820 --> 07:16.450
Let me guess, the colonel railroaded through, right?

07:16.450 --> 07:17.910
I'll keep it a secret.

07:18.540 --> 07:20.200
Thank you so much!

07:20.660 --> 07:24.120
But I wonder what he was looking up?

07:24.540 --> 07:25.210
Any idea?

07:26.790 --> 07:29.590
I don't know the details either,

07:30.300 --> 07:33.970
but he asked me whether there were
any documents concerning Research Laboratory 5.

07:35.220 --> 07:37.720
That, and the murder of Brigadier General Hughes...

07:39.970 --> 07:44.480
It's thanks to the Brigadier General that I got a job here.

07:44.480 --> 07:46.650
Ah, that's right.

07:49.270 --> 07:51.150
Well, there's a lot of work to do today as always.

07:53.030 --> 07:54.240
I'm counting on you.

07:55.910 --> 07:56.820
Yes, sir.

08:13.630 --> 08:14.970
Morning, Sheska.

08:15.220 --> 08:16.970
Yes? Huh?

08:17.640 --> 08:18.640
What?

08:37.320 --> 08:38.410
Hello.

08:44.620 --> 08:47.120
Did you perhaps lose some weight?

08:48.710 --> 08:49.920
I might have.

08:51.130 --> 08:52.340
You were injured?

08:52.750 --> 08:55.260
Just some trouble down south.

08:55.260 --> 08:57.720
It's just a scratch.

08:58.720 --> 08:59.640
I see.

09:00.850 --> 09:03.430
By the way, I met the Elric Brothers while I was down there.

09:04.350 --> 09:07.810
A coincidence. They were meeting their master, who lives in Dublith.

09:08.270 --> 09:09.310
Major.

09:09.310 --> 09:10.190
Yes?

09:11.610 --> 09:13.440
Have you told them about Hughes' death?

09:15.240 --> 09:17.950
No, I couldn't bring myself to tell them.

09:18.610 --> 09:20.450
They'll find out sooner or later.

09:20.820 --> 09:22.280
I know that, sir.

09:23.620 --> 09:26.160
Research Laboratory 5 and the philosopher's stones.

09:26.160 --> 09:27.960
The ingredients to the stones are live humans.

09:29.790 --> 09:31.750
He was such an accommodating guy.

09:32.210 --> 09:38.720
He probably stuck his nose into what the Elric Brothers were researching and uncovered something he shouldn't have.

09:39.300 --> 09:40.590
Is that why you won't tell them?

09:42.850 --> 09:49.060
If they find out Hughes died because he got involved with them, they'd be devastated...

09:50.650 --> 09:52.480
You're too kind.

09:54.230 --> 09:55.610
And you know too much.

09:55.860 --> 09:56.990
I'm almost there.

09:58.650 --> 09:59.990
Please be careful.

10:01.990 --> 10:05.490
No one knows who could be listening.

10:06.950 --> 10:08.250
I'll be going on ahead.

10:16.300 --> 10:18.420
Huh? Lieutenant Hawkeye!

10:20.470 --> 10:22.340
Ah, it's been a while.

10:23.800 --> 10:25.760
If you're here, that means...

10:25.760 --> 10:26.680
Sorry to make you wait.

10:27.810 --> 10:29.270
I knew it...

10:29.270 --> 10:30.690
Oh, Fullmetal.

10:30.690 --> 10:33.690
Why the hell are you here, Colonel?

10:33.690 --> 10:36.320
I was transferred to Central effective last month.

10:37.650 --> 10:39.690
And what about you? What brings you here?

10:40.820 --> 10:43.870
Just collecting some information.

10:44.240 --> 10:47.660
We were also thinking about going to say hi to Lt. Colonel Hughes.

10:48.290 --> 10:50.290
How's he doing?

10:53.120 --> 10:54.170
He's no longer here.

10:54.540 --> 10:55.290
Huh?

10:56.130 --> 10:57.920
He decided to retire to the country.

10:58.420 --> 11:03.180
He's going to take over the family business along with his wife and daughter.

11:03.890 --> 11:05.260
So he's not here.

11:06.180 --> 11:08.850
Oh... that's too bad.

11:08.850 --> 11:10.680
We were looking forward to seeing him, too...

11:14.400 --> 11:15.270
Fullmetal.

11:16.900 --> 11:20.070
Don't jump the gun and do anything reckless.

11:21.690 --> 11:22.570
Sure.

11:33.790 --> 11:36.130
Treating them like children only at a time like this?

11:36.840 --> 11:38.630
They don't need to know right now.

11:39.380 --> 11:43.970
It's better if there are fewer obstacles for those brothers to move forward.

11:44.800 --> 11:47.510
But they'll find out eventually.

11:49.720 --> 11:55.690
I don't have the right to call
Major Armstrong soft-hearted, either.

11:57.440 --> 11:59.900
Soft-hearted?

12:01.150 --> 12:02.320
Don't you mean cruel?

12:03.780 --> 12:05.820
So the Lt. Colonel isn't around, huh...

12:05.820 --> 12:08.320
Oh, I almost forgot, Brother.

12:08.320 --> 12:10.240
We have to let Winry know.

12:10.240 --> 12:12.040
She's headed for his home.

12:12.250 --> 12:13.500
You're right.

12:17.540 --> 12:18.500
Second Lieutenant Ross!

12:19.090 --> 12:21.170
It's been a while, you two.

12:21.170 --> 12:22.760
What's the hurry?

12:22.760 --> 12:25.260
We heard about Lt. Colonel Hughes, so...

12:27.510 --> 12:28.600
I see...

12:28.600 --> 12:29.510
It's hard, isn't it?

12:29.760 --> 12:32.270
There was so much I wanted to say to him, too...

12:32.680 --> 12:34.560
I wish we had a chance to have a proper farewell with him.

12:35.730 --> 12:37.730
No one contacted you about it, huh?

12:38.520 --> 12:39.770
Don't worry.

12:39.770 --> 12:42.110
The army gave him a proper farewell.

12:42.110 --> 12:44.320
Really? That's nice of you guys.

12:44.780 --> 12:45.950
Of course.

12:46.820 --> 12:53.700
Also, you may have heard this already, but he was specially promoted two ranks to the rank of Brigadier General.

12:54.370 --> 12:55.710
Specially promoted two ranks?

12:56.250 --> 12:58.630
He was specially promoted for retiring to the country?

13:05.300 --> 13:06.220
Second Lieutenant Ross!

13:23.530 --> 13:25.070
Here you go.

13:25.490 --> 13:26.440
Thanks.

13:31.820 --> 13:34.490
You can't be serious! Why was he...

13:34.490 --> 13:35.580
Why?!

13:43.000 --> 13:43.920
Brother!

13:45.760 --> 13:51.890
Brigadier General Hughes was murdered by someone soon after you were released from the hospital.

13:52.430 --> 13:55.100
They haven't caught the perpetrator yet.

13:57.770 --> 13:59.440
It's my fault...

13:59.440 --> 14:02.520
I dragged him into this! Lt. Colonel Hughes!

14:17.160 --> 14:19.250
Well, careful out there.

14:19.250 --> 14:22.210
Be sure to drop by if you ever come to Central again. 

14:22.210 --> 14:25.300
Oh, Alphonse, you can't eat with that armor on, can you? 

14:25.460 --> 14:28.630
You guys probably haven't booked a place to stay at yet, right? 

14:28.630 --> 14:30.300
If so, stay at my place. 

14:48.530 --> 14:49.400
Papa!

15:07.420 --> 15:08.550
What are you going to do?

15:09.210 --> 15:10.920
I'm going to tell them everything.

15:11.760 --> 15:12.970
You head back.

15:13.800 --> 15:16.510
I'm the only one who needs to face them.

15:18.310 --> 15:20.560
It's not just your problem.

15:20.560 --> 15:22.270
It concerns both of us.

15:22.810 --> 15:24.940
So I'm going, too.

15:26.400 --> 15:27.940
Hey, Al.

15:27.940 --> 15:28.730
What if-

15:28.730 --> 15:32.400
We chose to get our bodies back no matter what,

15:34.360 --> 15:38.790
but if people end up dying because of it, I'd rather not.

15:46.210 --> 15:47.710
Winry just came by, too...

15:48.210 --> 15:49.210
We know.

15:52.090 --> 15:52.920
Winry.

15:59.010 --> 16:03.940
There's something I need to tell you, Miss Gracia.

16:03.940 --> 16:05.140
Is that okay?

16:05.140 --> 16:06.440
Something to tell me?

16:06.440 --> 16:07.310
Yes.

16:08.310 --> 16:09.020
And to Winry, too.

16:14.240 --> 16:18.740
So my husband uncovered something about these philosopher's stones...

16:19.580 --> 16:25.500
And his death is the murderers' way of saying "don't meddle in our affairs"?

16:27.880 --> 16:30.590
We basically dragged him in.

16:30.590 --> 16:31.750
I'm so sorry.

16:36.800 --> 16:37.760
I'm terribly sorry...

16:40.560 --> 16:44.520
If he died while trying to help someone, then that's just like him.

16:45.730 --> 16:50.770
He's always been a meddling, accommodating kind of guy, and he'd always end up losing things due to his kindness.

16:52.280 --> 16:55.610
But I don't think he's ever regretted it.

16:56.490 --> 16:59.370
Even till the moment of his death.

17:00.870 --> 17:02.370
We're...

17:03.750 --> 17:05.960
Don't tell me you're going to give up.

17:07.960 --> 17:13.210
If you two give up here, it'd mean
my husband's death was completely meaningless.

17:15.840 --> 17:20.140
Even if it's impossible with the philosopher's stones, there may be other ways, right?

17:23.390 --> 17:24.850
Miss Gracia...

17:26.560 --> 17:30.940
Move forward on the path you're content with.

17:37.110 --> 17:38.200
Mama...

17:39.070 --> 17:41.200
Please don't cry, Mama...

18:41.970 --> 18:43.930
You're in there, right, Winry?

18:47.430 --> 18:49.890
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

18:50.600 --> 18:52.770
The dining hall's going to close soon.

18:53.600 --> 18:54.730
Okay...

18:54.730 --> 18:57.900
You won't be able to function without food.

18:58.400 --> 18:59.240
Yeah...

19:01.030 --> 19:03.320
Well, I'm heading back to my room.

19:08.540 --> 19:09.500
Apple pie?

19:11.000 --> 19:13.880
I practiced making it a few times since then.

19:15.040 --> 19:18.250
I don't mean to brag, but I've gotten really good at it.

19:19.880 --> 19:22.760
Well, it's nowhere near as good as Miss Gracia's, though...

19:24.390 --> 19:25.390
Someday...

19:27.310 --> 19:31.020
I wanted Mr. Hughes to try it.

19:49.290 --> 19:53.000
The Colonel is digging around
for information about Hughes' death?

19:53.000 --> 19:54.120
Yeah.

19:54.540 --> 19:56.500
I wonder if he's discovered anything?

19:57.170 --> 19:58.670
Maybe.

20:00.130 --> 20:01.010
What do we do?

20:01.590 --> 20:06.510
We moved him to Central to keep an eye on him...

20:07.010 --> 20:09.720
Can't he just behave?

20:09.720 --> 20:12.350
He's a precious candidate for sacrifice.

20:12.730 --> 20:15.350
You haven't gotten any information out of your boyfriend?

20:15.650 --> 20:17.230
Nothing.

20:17.230 --> 20:19.360
I can't even tell if he's foolish or able.

20:19.980 --> 20:22.190
I'll go hunt for some information again.

20:23.110 --> 20:25.200
We're going, Gluttony.

20:28.450 --> 20:32.120
Geez, Gluttony! Don't leave this place a mess!

20:32.120 --> 20:33.330
Seriously...

20:35.920 --> 20:37.500
Hey, Lust?

20:37.500 --> 20:40.880
We just need the Flame Alchemist to behave, right?

20:42.300 --> 20:43.130
That's right.

20:43.760 --> 20:46.380
Are you up for taking another measure?

20:48.470 --> 20:49.890
Got something on your mind?

20:50.760 --> 20:54.890
The best way to shut up an annoying dog is to give him some food.

20:59.360 --> 21:00.820
Second Lieutenant Maria Ross.

21:02.280 --> 21:05.240
I'm Henry Douglas from military police headquarters.

21:06.610 --> 21:07.860
Can I help you?

21:08.200 --> 21:09.740
You're coming with me.

21:10.490 --> 21:11.120
Your sidearm.

21:16.000 --> 21:17.580
Care to explain?

21:18.170 --> 21:23.210
Your name has been called as a
material witness in the murder of Maes Hughes.

21:24.460 --> 21:25.670
That's impossible!

21:25.920 --> 21:27.680
You can explain yourself later.

21:28.550 --> 21:29.180
Come with me.

21:33.100 --> 21:36.930
Second Lieutenant Maria Ross is denying all charges.

21:37.560 --> 21:40.100
Collect all data concerning her.

21:40.100 --> 21:41.270
Make it quick.

21:41.270 --> 21:42.820
However, do it in strict secrecy.

21:43.110 --> 21:44.110
Yes, sir!

21:53.780 --> 21:56.080
Hey lady, could you wrap up these flowers for me?

21:56.080 --> 21:59.330
Oh my, are you going on a date? You lady-killer!

22:14.720 --> 22:16.350
Did I make you wait, Solaris?

22:17.980 --> 22:20.100
No, I just got here.

22:20.690 --> 22:22.440
I've been dying to see you, Jean.

22:23.150 --> 22:25.730
I'm looking forward to hearing your interesting stories again.

22:33.330 --> 22:37.420
I don't have to act tough, right?

22:33.330 --> 22:37.420
Tsuyogaranakute iindane

22:38.670 --> 22:44.220
The scribbling someone made...

22:38.670 --> 22:44.220
Dareka ga kaitetta

22:44.220 --> 22:50.020
On the wall, of a flower is swaying.

22:44.220 --> 22:50.020
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:50.020 --> 22:55.600
No one knows their true selves.

22:50.020 --> 22:55.600
Jibunrashisa nante dermo wakaranaiyo

22:55.600 --> 22:57.900
Even though we both lose and gain

22:55.600 --> 22:57.900
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu de

22:57.900 --> 23:01.320
By embarking on this long, long path,

22:57.900 --> 23:01.320
Nakushitari hirottari

23:01.320 --> 23:08.990
And though there may be days loneliness strikes and makes us weep...

23:01.320 --> 23:08.990
Kyuu ni samishikunatte naichau hi mo arukedo

23:11.080 --> 23:16.500
Let's transform our tears and pains to stars.

23:11.080 --> 23:16.500
Namida mo itami mo hoshi ni kaeyou

23:16.500 --> 23:22.500
Let's light a candle to illuminate our tomorrow.

23:16.500 --> 23:22.500
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:22.500 --> 23:27.630
And we'll hold our small hands over the fire to create stardust,

23:22.500 --> 23:27.630
Chiisana te kazashite futari de tsukurou

23:27.630 --> 23:32.850
And an eternity that shines so brilliantly.

23:27.630 --> 23:32.850
Hoshikuzu wo tsuyoku hikaru eien wo

23:32.850 --> 23:38.230
Farewells may be unavoidable,

23:32.850 --> 23:38.230
Sayonara itsuka wa kurukamoshirenai

23:38.230 --> 23:44.150
Yet the seasons continue to change obliviously.

23:38.230 --> 23:44.150
Kisetsu wa soredemo meguri megutteku

23:44.480 --> 23:48.240
Even if I lose myself, I'll continue to walk...

23:44.480 --> 23:48.240
Chiisaku mayottemo aruiteku

23:48.240 --> 23:52.280
Walk by your side.

23:48.240 --> 23:52.280
Kimi to aruiteku

23:52.280 --> 23:56.580
That's the only thing I'd like to never change.

23:52.280 --> 23:56.580
Sore dake wa kawaranaideiyoune

23:59.520 --> 24:03.770
The sacrificial lamb is engulfed in the flames of hatred...

24:03.770 --> 24:07.530
...and leaves the boy with feelings of hate and regret.

24:08.280 --> 24:12.530
And the man reaches out to the darkness.

24:13.660 --> 24:17.790
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

24:17.790 --> 24:20.790
Cold Flame

24:17.790 --> 24:20.790
Episode 17, Cold Flame.

24:21.540 --> 24:25.840
All is playing into the hands of the unknown.
